hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20592","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu Qilabah used to narrate this hadith to me, then said to me: Would you like the one who narrated it to me? So he directed me to him, and I came to him, and he said: A relative of mine called Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning camels of a neighbor of mine that were seized, and I found him eating, and he invited me to his food, and I said: I am fasting. He said: Come near, or: Come, I shall tell you about that: Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, has lifted fasting and half the prayer from the traveler, and from the pregnant and nursing woman. He said: After that he used to grieve, saying: Would that I had eaten of the food of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he invited me to it."
"20593","'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Sawadah al-Qushayri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, one of Banu Ka'b, brother of Banu Qushayr, he said: The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raided us, so I set out to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and reached him while he was eating, and said to me: Come near and eat. So I said: I am fasting, then he mentioned the hadith."
